# Colorscapes

A minimal WebGL-based gradient editor. No dependencies, no bundlers, no build tools, no tests — just plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript.

## Overview

Colorscapes lets you build multi-layered gradients out of custom shapes. You can tweak color stops, adjust blend modes and blur, and export the result as a PNG.

## Features

**Shapes.** Each shape has its own position, rotation, corner rounding, and softness. Stack as many as you need.

**Color stops.** Add, remove, and reorder stops per shape.

**Blending.** A two-pass blur softens overlaps between layers, and you can pick from a range of compositing modes to mix them.

**Export.** High-resolution PNG output, ready to drop into a design.

**Shareable URLs.** The full gradient state is encoded in the URL hash, so a link restores the exact design.

**Presets.** Start from a built-in preset or generate something random, and save your own — custom presets persist in `localStorage` between sessions.

## Requirements

A modern browser with WebGL. If WebGL is unavailable, the app shows an error message instead of failing silently.